---
import MotionPage from '@/components/MotionPage.astro';
import Code from '@/components/Code.astro';
import { MotionPresenceReact } from '@/examples/react/motion-presence.tsx';
import { MotionPresenceAngular } from '@/examples/angular/motion-presence.ts';
import MotionPresenceSvelte from '@/examples/svelte/motion-presence.svelte';
import reactSource from '@/examples/react/motion-presence.tsx?raw';
import angularSource from '@/examples/angular/motion-presence.ts?raw';
import svelteSource from '@/examples/svelte/motion-presence.svelte?raw';
import { buttonClass, cardClass, demoClass } from '@/components/motionDemo';
---
<MotionPage title="Motion: presence" description="Entries and exits of elements: the hidden attribute, data-presence, focus restoration and the framework adapters.">
  <h1>Presence</h1>
  <p>A presence motion makes an element enter when it is inserted or shown, and leave when it is hidden or removed. It has the verbs <code>appear</code> (the entry, which leaves backward) and <code>disappear</code>. Its name goes in <code>data-motion</code>, and the runtime does the rest.</p>

  <h2>Define</h2>
  <pre><code>{`import { defineMotion } from '@udixio/motion';

defineMotion('panel-enter', {
  verb: 'appear',
  keyframes: [
    { opacity: 0, y: 16 },
    { opacity: 1, y: 0 },
  ],
});`}</code></pre>

  <h2>HTML</h2>
  <pre><code>{`<section data-motion="slide">Enters when inserted</section>

// Hide: plays the exit. The attribute stays, and the element is inert until the exit ends.
panel.hidden = true;
// Show again: plays the entry.
panel.hidden = false;`}</code></pre>
  <ul>
    <li>An inserted element plays its entry, unless it is inserted with <code>hidden</code>.</li>
    <li>Setting <code>hidden</code> plays the exit. The element stays displayed and <code>inert</code> until the exit ends.</li>
    <li>Removing <code>hidden</code> plays the entry.</li>
    <li>An element that is on the page when the runtime connects plays no entry.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The state of the element</h2>
  <p>The runtime writes <code>data-presence="entering" | "present" | "exiting"</code> on each element with a presence motion. Authors do not set it; they style it, for example with <code>data-[presence=exiting]:pointer-events-none</code>.</p>

  <h2>Try it</h2>
  <p>A card with the <code>slide</code> preset, and a button that hides or shows it.</p>
  <div class={demoClass}>
    <button type="button" class={buttonClass} data-presence-toggle aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="presence-card">Hide the card</button>
    <div id="presence-card" data-motion="slide" class={cardClass}>This card enters and leaves with its exit.</div>
  </div>

  <h2>Focus (WCAG 2.4.3)</h2>
  <p>An exit sets <code>inert</code> on its element, and the browser then drops focus that was inside it. When the exit starts with focus inside, name where focus goes:</p>
  <pre><code>{`<div data-motion="fade" data-motion-restore-focus="#open-button">…</div>`}</code></pre>
  <p>The selector is looked up in the document when the exit starts, and focus moves to the element it matches before <code>inert</code> is set. In JavaScript, the same is the <code>restoreFocus</code> option, an element or a function that gives one: <code>motion(panel, 'fade', &#123; restoreFocus: () =&gt; opener &#125;)</code>. Without a target, the element stays focusable until focus leaves it or the exit ends, and development logs a warning once per element.</p>

  <h2>JavaScript</h2>
  <pre><code>{`import { motion } from '@udixio/motion';
import '@udixio/motion/presets';

const binding = motion(panel, 'slide', { settled: true }); // present, no entry
console.log(await binding.setPresent(false)); // 'finished' or 'cancelled'
await binding.setPresent(true);`}</code></pre>
  <p><code>setPresent(present)</code> runs the exit or the entry and resolves to <code>'finished'</code> or <code>'cancelled'</code>. It never rejects.</p>

  <h2>In the frameworks</h2>
  <p>The live examples below render a card with the <code>slide</code> preset. The framework keeps the card in place until its exit has played.</p>
  <Code codes={{ react: reactSource, angular: angularSource, svelte: svelteSource }}>
    <MotionPresenceReact slot="react" client:only="react" />
    <MotionPresenceAngular slot="angular" client:load />
    <MotionPresenceSvelte slot="svelte" client:only="svelte" />
  </Code>
  <p>React: <code>useMotion(source, &#123; present &#125;)</code>, with <code>mounted</code> true while the exit plays. Angular: add <code>Motion</code> to <code>imports</code>; <code>[udxMotionPresent]</code> sets the presence. Svelte: <code>&#123;&#64;attach motion('slide')&#125; transition:presence</code>.</p>

  <h2>Hydrated server content</h2>
  <p>React treats server-rendered content as already in place, so it plays no entry on hydration. An element marked <code>data-presence="present"</code> (the Angular server render marks its present elements) is bound settled, whatever the framework. <code>settled: false</code> asks for the entry anyway.</p>

  <h2>Reduced motion</h2>
  <p>Under reduced motion (<code>prefers-reduced-motion: reduce</code>, or <code>data-motion-policy="reduce"</code> on <code>html</code>), an entry and an exit become a short opacity fade. With <code>--udx-motion: none</code> on the element or an ancestor, the end state applies at once. See <a href="/motion/accessibility">Accessibility</a>.</p>

  <h2>Limits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A presence motion's element must accept a DOM reference in the framework; a component that does not forward its ref cannot be animated.</li>
    <li>A cancelled motion releases nothing, so the next motion carries from where it stopped.</li>
    <li>A value that is not neutral stays inline at the end of a motion (the <code>opacity</code> 0 of an exit, for instance), so a class that sets the same property is overridden until the binding is destroyed (see <a href="/motion/limits">Limits</a>).</li>
  </ul>

  <script>
    document.addEventListener('click', event => {
      if (!(event.target instanceof Element)) return;
      const toggle = event.target.closest<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-presence-toggle]');
      if (!toggle) return;
      const card = document.getElementById('presence-card');
      if (!card) return;
      const hide = !card.hidden;
      card.hidden = hide;
      toggle.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(!hide));
      toggle.textContent = hide ? 'Show the card' : 'Hide the card';
    });
  </script>
</MotionPage>
